<title>ITALY: Caio resigns as CEO at Italy's Olivetti.</title>
<headline>Caio resigns as CEO at Italy's Olivetti.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN, Italy</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's struggling Olivetti said Wednesday that Chief Executive Officer Francesco Caio had resigned at an extraordinary board meeting and would be replaced by Roberto Colaninno.</p>
<p>Colaninno is currently managing director of automotive group Sogefi, which is owned by Olivetti's ex-chairman Carlo De Benedetti's CIR industrial holding company.</p>
